# Cursor Cloud Agent (Cross-Project Run Contract)

Use this same contract for every repo to keep local AI behavior consistent.

## Start of each session
1) Confirm current branch and sync: `git status` then `git pull`.
2) Quick sanity check: `git branch --show-current` and review `README.md`.
3) Setup:
   - If `npm run setup:local` exists: `npm run setup:local`
   - Else run `npm ci` (or `npm install` if lockfile not present)
4) Run app:
   - If `npm run dev:local` exists: `npm run dev:local`
   - Else if `npm run dev` exists: `npm run dev`
5) Validate:
   - If `npm run verify:local` exists: `npm run verify:local`
   - Else run `npm run lint` when present, then `npm run build` when present.
6) For native flows, if scripts exist, run `npm run native:sync`, then `npm run native:ios` or `npm run native:android`.

## Collaboration rules
- Keep existing functionality intact.
- Keep file edits minimal and scoped.
- Do not commit secrets. Use `.env.local` / project secret store.
- Before changing API, data, or checkout/payment flow, ask for approval.
- Keep all local model handoff notes in `docs/handoff-lm-studio-cursor.md` when requested.

## Preferred handoff artifacts
- `docs/local-ai-runbook.md` if present
- `local-runner-profile.json` if present
- `README.md` run instructions
- `.env.example` for required environment variables

